.TH SMARTIMAGEDIFF 1 "2026-09-03" "smartmet-library-regression" "SmartMet Regression Tools"
.SH NAME
smartimagediff \- structural, anti\(hyaliasing\(hyaware image regression check
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smartimagediff
.I result
.I expected
.RI [ overlay.png ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B smartimagediff
compares two images and judges on the
.I geometry
of the surviving differences instead of on their average. A global
metric such as the PSNR of
.BR smartimagediff_psnr (1)
cannot separate sub\(hypixel anti\(hyaliasing and font\(hyhinting jitter
spread thinly over every edge \(em which must be tolerated, for example
when the accepted image was rendered on another OS or freetype version
\(em from a spatially clustered solid change such as a missing glyph or
a dropped map feature, which must be caught. Both can produce the same
average error, and a real change may well score
.I better
than harmless noise.
.PP
The comparison proceeds in five steps:
.RS 4
.IP 1. 4
per\(hypixel YIQ perceptual colour delta (pixelmatch / Yee metric);
.IP 2. 4
anti\(hyaliasing\(hyclass pixels are discarded (Vy\(vsniauskas detector);
.IP 3. 4
only high\(hyamplitude differences are kept \(em a dark glyph on a light
isoband is a large colour delta, whereas font\(hyhinting jitter is a
small gray\(hyversus\(hygray edge delta;
.IP 4. 4
the surviving pixels are clustered with 8\(hyconnectivity;
.IP 5. 4
the verdict is a failure if and only if some cluster is large enough.
Rendering jitter only ever produces thin per\(hyedge specks, while a real
change forms one solid blob.
.RE
.PP
Images of differing dimensions are always a failure.
.PP
As a guard against a sub\(hypixel change that the per\(hypixel detector
cannot distinguish from stationary anti\(hyaliasing \(em a thin line that
moved by about one pixel along its whole length, for instance a
simplified coastline \(em the result is also a failure when the
anti\(hyaliasing\(hyclassified pixels exceed both
.B SID_AA_FLOOD_MIN
pixels and
.B SID_MAX_AA_FRACTION
of the image area. Genuine anti\(hyaliasing stays a thin fringe;
a displacement floods a far larger share. Requiring both conditions
avoids false positives on small images (high fraction but few pixels)
and on huge sparse ones (many pixels, tiny fraction). Such a run is
marked with
.B aa_flood
in the output.
.PP
When the optional
.I overlay.png
argument is given, a human\(hyfacing difference image is written there:
the
.I expected
image faded to faint grayscale with the significant changes painted red
and boxed, so the eye lands directly on the regression instead of
scanning the equalized full\(hyframe of edge noise that a plain
difference image produces.
.PP
.BR smartpngdiff (1)
runs this program alongside the PSNR measurement; see there for how the
two verdicts are combined.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I result
Image produced by the test under inspection.
.TP
.I expected
Accepted reference image.
.TP
.I overlay.png
Optional output path for the red\(hyboxed difference overlay.
.SH OUTPUT
One line on standard output, for example:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
OK    largest_cluster=6 clusters=2 changed_px=11 aa_ignored=843
FAIL  largest_cluster=214 clusters=3 changed_px=402 aa_ignored=915 at=[512,233 46x18]
FAIL  size mismatch 1024x768
.fi
.RE
.PP
.TP
.B largest_cluster
Area in pixels of the biggest surviving cluster \(em the number the
verdict is based on.
.TP
.B clusters
Number of clusters at or above the noise floor
.RB ( SID_MIN_CLUSTER ).
.TP
.B changed_px
Total number of pixels in those clusters.
.TP
.B aa_ignored
Candidate pixels discarded as anti\(hyaliasing.
.TP
.B at=[x,y wxh]
Bounding box of the biggest cluster, printed when one exists.
.TP
.B aa_flood
The anti\(hyaliasing flood guard described above triggered.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The thresholds are tunable; the defaults were chosen on the WMS
regression suite and should rarely need changing.
.TP
.B SID_THRESHOLD
Base per\(hypixel YIQ sensitivity (default
.BR 0.1 ).
.TP
.B SID_STRONG
Normalized amplitude above which a pixel counts as significant (default
.BR 0.25 ).
Raising it past about 0.30 starts dropping real glyph signal.
.TP
.B SID_MIN_CLUSTER
Clusters smaller than this many pixels are counted as noise (default
.BR 8 ).
.TP
.B SID_FAIL_CLUSTER
Any surviving cluster of at least this many pixels is a regression
(default
.BR 80 ).
.TP
.B SID_MAX_AA_FRACTION
Fraction of the image area above which anti\(hyaliasing\(hyclassified
pixels are treated as a flood (default
.BR 0.003 ,
that is 0.3%). Set to
.B 0
or less to disable the guard.
.TP
.B SID_AA_FLOOD_MIN
Absolute floor of anti\(hyaliasing\(hyclassified pixels below which the
fraction is not trusted (default
.BR 1000 ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No regression found.
.TP
.B 1
Regression found, or the images differ in size.
.TP
.B 2
Wrong number of arguments, or an image could not be read
.RB ( "Error: " \fImessage\fR
on standard error).
.SH EXAMPLES
Check a result against its reference:
.PP
.RS 4
smartimagediff results/contour.png results_ok/contour.png
.RE
.PP
Write the red\(hyboxed overlay as well, and be stricter about cluster
size:
.PP
.RS 4
SID_FAIL_CLUSTER=40 smartimagediff results/contour.png \\
.br
.RS 0
.RE
.RS 4
results_ok/contour.png results_diff/contour.png
.RE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smartpngdiff (1),
.BR smartimagediff_psnr (1),
.BR magick (1)
.PP
The rationale, the measured PSNR\(hyversus\(hycluster separation and the
tuning notes are in
.B docs/structural-image-diff.md
of the
.B smartmet-library-regression
sources.
.SH AUTHOR
Finnish Meteorological Institute
.PP
Report issues at <https://github.com/fmidev/smartmet-library-regression/issues>.
